Check contextual compatibility BEFORE additions. Both addition kinds NONE does
not imply equivalence: a supported context_conflict independently gives NO/NO.
If a unique prefix/suffix reverses a shared claim, cite that modifier on its side
and the shared assertion on the other. Do not invent a missing unique loss span.
Then assess unique content: A's addition prevents B replacing A, and vice versa.
The same-record and non-main-only vetoes do not apply. Proper subset direction
does not depend on severity. Titles/navigation alone are not role conflicts.

